  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Top reference line: horizontal straight line of length L between two filled black endpoint dots",
    "Double-headed dimension arrow above the top line with vertical end ticks, labeled 'L'",
    "Labels 'Node' beneath each endpoint dot of the top reference line",
    "Four stacked standing-wave panels on lines of identical length L, one per mode",
    "Left-hand mode labels: 'n = 1', 'n = 2', 'n = 3', 'n = 4'",
    "Dark blue sinusoidal curve in each panel (instantaneous string shape)",
    "Pale blue mirror-image curve in each panel (opposite phase, outlining the oscillation envelope)",
    "Filled black dots marking the pinned endpoints of every wave panel",
    "Interior crossing points (nodes): 0 for n=1, 1 for n=2, 2 for n=3, 3 for n=4",
    "Right-hand fit equations: '1/2 lambda_1 = L', 'lambda_2 = L', '3/2 lambda_3 = L', '4/2 lambda_4 = L'",
    "Right-hand wavelength results: 'lambda_1 = 2/1 L', 'lambda_2 = 2/2 L', 'lambda_3 = 2/3 L', 'lambda_4 = 2/4 L'",
    "General expression at lower right: 'lambda_n = 2/n L' with 'n = 1, 2, 3, . . .'",
    "Optional highlight annotations: node markers and antinode markers on the selected mode"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "modeSelect",
      "type": "state",
      "label": "Mode number n",
      "states": ["n=1", "n=2", "n=3", "n=4"],
      "default": "n=1",
      "teaches": "Each successive mode packs one more half-wavelength into the same fixed length, adding one interior node and shortening the wavelength to 2L/n."
    },
    {
      "id": "oscillate",
      "type": "animation",
      "label": "Play string oscillation",
      "loop": true,
      "teaches": "The pale and dark curves are the same string at opposite phases: nodes never move while antinodes swing through the full envelope."
    },
    {
      "id": "lengthL",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "String length L",
      "range": [0.5, 2.0, 0.05],
      "default": 1.0,
      "teaches": "Wavelength scales directly with string length at fixed n, so lambda_n = 2L/n holds for any string."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The fixed string",
      "narration": "A string of length L is clamped at both ends; those clamped points can never move, so they are permanent nodes. Every allowed wave must start and end at zero displacement.",
      "state": { "modeSelect": "n=1", "lengthL": 1.0, "oscillate": false }
    },
    {
      "title": "Fundamental: one half-wavelength",
      "narration": "The simplest fit is a single hump with no interior nodes: exactly half a wavelength spans L, so 1/2 lambda_1 = L and lambda_1 = 2L.",
      "state": { "modeSelect": "n=1", "lengthL": 1.0, "oscillate": false }
    },
    {
      "title": "Watch it vibrate",
      "narration": "Playing the motion shows the string sweeping between the dark and pale curves. The endpoints stay pinned while the centre antinode moves the most.",
      "state": { "modeSelect": "n=1", "lengthL": 1.0, "oscillate": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Second harmonic",
      "narration": "Fit two half-wavelengths and a node appears at the midpoint. Now lambda_2 = L — half the fundamental wavelength on the same string.",
      "state": { "modeSelect": "n=2", "lengthL": 1.0, "oscillate": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Third and fourth harmonics",
      "narration": "Three and then four half-wavelengths fit, giving two and three interior nodes and wavelengths 2L/3 and 2L/4. Only whole numbers of half-wavelengths are permitted.",
      "state": { "modeSelect": "n=4", "lengthL": 1.0, "oscillate": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Stretch the string",
      "narration": "Dragging L longer stretches every mode's wavelength in proportion while the number of nodes stays fixed, confirming lambda_n = 2L/n.",
      "state": { "modeSelect": "n=3", "lengthL": 1.8, "oscillate": true }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Boundary conditions quantize the wave: because both ends must be nodes, only wavelengths that fit a whole number of half-waves into L survive, so lambda_n = 2L/n.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Vertical stack of five panels on a white background, all sharing the same horizontal span. Top panel: a plain straight line between two small filled black dots labeled 'Node' below each end, with a thin double-headed arrow above it terminated by short vertical ticks and labeled 'L' at its centre. Below it, four evenly spaced wave panels labeled at the far left in italic serif as n = 1 through n = 4. Each panel shows a medium-dark steel-blue sinusoid and its light pale-blue mirror image, together forming a lens/envelope shape; both curves are pinned to black dots at the two ends, and they cross at n-1 interior points. Amplitude is the same for all modes. To the right of each panel, two math expressions in serif type, spaced apart: the fit condition (1/2 lambda_1 = L, lambda_2 = L, 3/2 lambda_3 = L, 4/2 lambda_4 = L) and the wavelength result (lambda_n = 2/n L form). Lower right of the whole figure carries the general rule lambda_n = 2/n L with n = 1, 2, 3, . . . . In the interactive version, the currently selected mode panel is highlighted (others dimmed), animated by interpolating the dark curve between the two envelopes with a sine-in-time factor, with small hollow circles marking nodes and small arrows or brackets marking antinodes on the active mode; the shared line length rescales horizontally with the L slider and the L dimension arrow rescales with it."
}

