      "teaches": "Wavelength scales directly with string length at fixed n, so lambda_n = 2L/n holds for any string."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The fixed string",
      "narration": "A string of length L is clamped at both ends; those clamped points can never move, so they are permanent nodes. Every allowed wave must start and end at zero displacement.",
      "state": {
        "modeSelect": "n=1",
        "lengthL": 1,
        "oscillate": false
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Fundamental: one half-wavelength",
      "narration": "The simplest fit is a single hump with no interior nodes: exactly half a wavelength spans L, so 1/2 lambda_1 = L and lambda_1 = 2L.",
      "state": {
        "modeSelect": "n=1",
        "lengthL": 1,
        "oscillate": false
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Watch it vibrate",
      "narration": "Playing the motion shows the string sweeping between the dark and pale curves. The endpoints stay pinned while the centre antinode moves the most.",
      "state": {
        "modeSelect": "n=1",
        "lengthL": 1,
        "oscillate": true
      }
    },
    {
