      "state": {
        "modeSelect": "n=2",
        "lengthL": 1,
        "oscillate": true
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Third and fourth harmonics",
      "narration": "Three and then four half-wavelengths fit, giving two and three interior nodes and wavelengths 2L/3 and 2L/4. Only whole numbers of half-wavelengths are permitted.",
      "state": {
        "modeSelect": "n=4",
        "lengthL": 1,
        "oscillate": true
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Stretch the string",
      "narration": "Dragging L longer stretches every mode's wavelength in proportion while the number of nodes stays fixed, confirming lambda_n = 2L/n.",
      "state": {
        "modeSelect": "n=3",
        "lengthL": 1.8,
        "oscillate": true
      }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "Boundary conditions quantize the wave: because both ends must be nodes, only wavelengths that fit a whole number of half-waves into L survive, so lambda_n = 2L/n.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Vertical stack of five panels on a white background, all sharing the same horizontal span. Top panel: a plain straight line between two small filled black dots labeled 'Node' below each end, with a thin double-headed arrow above it terminated by short vertical ticks and labeled 'L' at its centre. Below it, four evenly spaced wave panels labeled at the far left in italic serif as n = 1 through n = 4. Each panel shows a medium-dark steel-blue sinusoid and its light pale-blue mirror image, together forming a lens/envelope shape; both curves are pinned to black dots at the two ends, and they cross at n-1 interior points. Amplitude is the same for all modes. To the right of each panel, two math expressions in serif type, spaced apart: the fit condition (1/2 lambda_1 = L, lambda_2 = L, 3/2 lambda_3 = L, 4/2 lambda_4 = L) and the wavelength result (lambda_n = 2/n L form). Lower right of the whole figure carries the general rule lambda_n = 2/n L with n = 1, 2, 3, . . . . In the interactive version, the currently selected mode panel is highlighted (others dimmed), animated by interpolating the dark curve between the two envelopes with a sine-in-time factor, with small hollow circles marking nodes and small arrows or brackets marking antinodes on the active mode; the shared line length rescales horizontally with the L slider and the L dimension arrow rescales with it."
}

